Organization: UBPG
Mime-Version: 1.0
Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1

It sounds to me like you're attempting to use the PrintServer accounting
utility with the Digital UNIX "pac" accounting file. 

PrintServer printers can generate separate, and much more detailed accounting
data files.  When you created the Management Client for this printer, you
should have been asked if you wanted accounting and event logging enabled.
The files are usually stored in /var/adm/<printername>.cact.  If you're
not sure if PrintServer accounting is enabled, please use the /etc/lpssetup
utility to look at the Management Client configuration.  If it's not 
set, Modify the Management Client with lpssetup and wait until a few jobs
have been printed then try using lpspac with the <printername>.cact file.

For more extensive information about PrintServer accounting, please check
your documentation (which is also included as .ps files in the /usr/opt/LPS
directory.

Lastly, to look at the accounting information collected from lpr (which is 
the file you mention in your post), check out the man page for pac (printer
accounting).  The PrintServer one gives you more detailed information, like
paper sizes, but if you're only looking for page counts, pac will do you fine.

Sue Gleeson




