Mark Paede wrote:
> 
> Hello!
> 
> I'm very new to DU and have a few questions regarding the Disk
> Configuration Utility:
> 1. The tool (configure partitions) looks a bit like Partition Magic,
> so I had the idea that it might be possible to change the sizes of the
> partitions "on the fly". After pressing the "apply" button, there is a
> warning message of possible data loss. Is this a _possible_ loss, or
> will the data on the changed partitions be lost?
> And if it should work without what is the possability of data-loss
> -more like 10 or like 90%?

If there was data on the partition, your damage could range from "no effect" to
"no data". When UNIX creates a file system, U makes it for that particular
partition size and offset. Increase the partition and the FS remains the same.
Move the partition and the FS is mis-located.

> 2. What happens if the DU starts without or with a changed
> swap-partition?

Not sure. Some versions stated that the swap is UFS type, but thats stupid. Swap
is just a partition, a range of blocks on the disk, where UNIX swaps memory
pages. And it is created every time machine boots (swapon).

> As the preinstalled swap partition is to small I would like to change
> it (see 1.) or I have to create a new one. So is it possible with just
> this utility to delete the old and create a new swap partition or do I
> have to change something else?

When you boot the DU4.0D CD, you can adjust any partitions for your
configuration. My choice is:

part	offset	size		purpose
----------------------------------------------------------
a	0	64-128 MB	root partition + bootstrap
b	a+	(2-3)xRAM	swap
c	0	0		unused
d	0	0		unused
e	0	0		unused
f	0	0		unused
g	a+b+	<rest>		usr + var
h	0	0		unused

And after I have done this, I choose advanced setup and procede.

Nix.




