Andre Laframboise (Andre.Laframboise@nlc-bnc.ca) wrote:

: Does anyone know where I can get info on the jumpers
: to set the SCSI id, termination, etc ?

Someone who I can't identify from the e-mail sent me this diagram which
I've used in the past to get RZ26s running out of a storage works (for
example, my 'test' Linux/Alpha system).

    +------------------------XXX+
    X<-----Pin 1            /   |
    X J6                   /    x
    X                     J5    xSCSI Connector
    |                           x
    |                           x
    |                  J2       |
    +----------------xxxxx------+                   +-------Pin 1
                       ^                            |
                       |                            v
                       +------------- . . . . . . . .
                                      . . . . . . . .
                                      R D M W P T T T
                                      E S E P E E P P
                                      S
                                        ^ ^
                                        /  \
                       Delayed Spin-up-+    +---Enable Motor Start
    DS  ME
    Off Off     Spindle starts immediately after power up (Default Setting)
    Off On      Spindle doesn't start till after Host "Start Unit" command
    On  Off     Spindle start delayed by SCSI ID Times 12 secs after Powerup
    On  On      Drive spindle starts when Start Unit command received from
                Host.....delayed start is overridden
    TP (Pin 1)  Term Power *TO* SCSI Bus
    TP (Pin 3)  Term Power *FROM* drive
    TE          Enable Terminators
    PE          Parity Option
    WP          Write Protect

    Drives are shipped with TP, TP, PE and ME installed

    SCSI ID is determined by J6 (or J5)
                 +-----------+
                 |* * * * * *|<---Pin 1
                 |* * * * * *|
                 +-----------+
                  A A A S L R         Drive ID (eg 5 = A2 and A0 installed)
                  2 1 0 S E E         SSP = Spindle Sync
                        P D S         RES = Reserved

    If  you  use  J5 for SCSI ID, A2 are the pair of pins closest to the
    SCSI Connector
