There were several problems getting XEmacs to build on DU. I have been 
running 20.4 and many, many 21.0 bets releases.

21.0 should build just fine "out of the box" on DU. I have not had a
build problem for any beta release for the past 6 months. I hope 21.0
is released soon, but the lead developer for XEmacs lost his job and
has limited Internet access, so it's bee pretty slow going.

You can get the latest beta if you want to. Of course, it is beta, but 
it is VERY close to being released.

For configuration with DU4.0, I suggest:
configure --without-gcc --cflags="-O3 -std" --site-includes=/usr/local/include
I also suggest gmake, in which case you would add "--with-gnu-make"
For 3.2, use gcc.

There is a problem with compiling etags. It required a minor
hack. It's fixed in 21.0. Also, if you use tpu-edt mode, the version
now distributed for 21.0 is the first in a while without known
problems. 
