Nicholas Guido wrote:
> 
> I recently upgraded sendmail.  I have created the configuration files to
> what I thought was right, but the mail server is now unable to send mail
> outside of our system.  The mail.log file gives error messages saying
> "Relaying denied".  Any help would be appreciated, I'm not too familiar
> with Sendmail.
> 

In your /etc/mail/access file, add the line:

Your.domain	RELAY

and then make the database. The command will vary according to the
type that you specified in your config files (m4 and cf). In my case
the sendmail.cf file has the following line:

Kaccess dbm  /etc/mail/access

and my command for making the data base (from the /etc/mail dir) is:

makemap dbm access<access

Note that it is also possible to use the relay-domains database.

RTFM (-:

Charlie

