Hi,

We have problems in printing via the Ethernet TCP/IP-Interface of
the HP LaserJet/JetDirect 4000 TN:

There are a lot of clients (Win NT, Win 95, VMS etc.) which  are not
directly sending the job to the printer, but using ONE printer queue 
at an Digital Workstation running with DEC-UNIX 4.0 D.

If the printer is idle and a new job sent, anything works correct. The
job is spooled at the (LPR-)queue and the queue sends it via TCP/IP to
the printer.

If the printer is busy and one (or more) job(s) comes, it will be stored
in the queue first until  the printer is ready. But instead of sending
the next job to the printer, ALL jobs which are queued will be deleted
at this time.
After that, the next job send to the idle-queue will be forwarded to
the printer in the right way.

Is this a problem of the HP Printer or our model in special, or a
general/configuration problem of DEC/OSF-LPR ?

Thanks for your help !

Philipp Pallo.

Please copy your answer to my mail: pallo@physnet.uni-hamburg.de
- Thanks ! -





