	Iwao Makino <smurf@cosm.co.jp> writes:

 
> anyone know if CAP is up to date? 

I'm not sure how up to date CAP is, but we have CAP 6.0 running fairly 
happily on a few Digital Unix 4.0D boxes here.  By fairly, I mean on a 
couple of occasions it's needed to be killed and restarted for some
unknown reason.  It runs with fast ethernet and we've even had it
running on an FDDI controller.
 
 
> PS: I may have to patch like 200 to satisfy those customers who does not want
> to pay $6k license...:(

The patch application isn't really too bad, a simple script is all that's 
required (I think they even supply an example).

There are a couple of gotchas like ensuring you have the PACKETFILTER option
compiled into your kernel and I remember there being a problem with the make
