> Morten Toftgaard Jensen wrote:
> 
> Hi there
> 
> I have a customer that wishes to have the mails sent by the system to
> root (errors, currently read in mailx) forwarded to a standard SMTP mail
> host. How may we solve this?
> 
> Thanks in advance for your answers !

1. Create a /.forward file with 600 perms, that contains the address
   that is supposed to receive the mail.

2. Create an entry in /var/adm/sendmail/aliases and run `newaliases`

3. Modify /etc/syslog.conf to redirect syslog reporting.

