In article <weber-0311981345480001@spinel.bucknell.edu>,
weber@bucknell.edu (Chris Weber) wrote:

>  There's a problem, though.  Any authorization created *after* the
>auto-migrate can't be modified by either  usermod  or  userdel .  Any
>attempt to apply either of these applications to a post-4.0D authorization
>results in the message:
>
>                    Specified user not found
>  [...]
>  Can anyone shed any light on this odd behavior?  I'm perplexed.
>
>  Thanks in advance for any help.

  Well, I stumbled upon the answer.  It seems there was an empty line
between two entries in /etc/passwd.  Mkpasswd ignores the empty line when
creating the /etc/passwd DBM files, but user{del,mod} apparently considers
the empty line as EOF during its scan for the requested username.  This
sort of thing isn't particularly easy to find as there's no other
indication anywhere that there's anything wrong.

  Sigh.

-- 
