Piotr Konieczny wrote:

>    We are running Digital Unix 4.0B on Alpha Server 2100 4/275. From time
> to time there is 'zombie' and I don't know how to remove it. 'kill -9' and
> rm /proc/pid don't work.

Check the process' parent process ID (PPID).  Frequently, zombies are
caused by the parent being hung and not doing a wait when it should. 
Or, it has a bug.  You'll need to find out what the process was in order
to track down the problem.



