Silke Mueller wrote:

> I'm searching for a debugger that is able to do threads and will run on
> a dec alpha with digital unix 4.0 (B or D). Free software would be
> appreciated, but commercial products are welcome as well.

I don't know of any thread-aware debugger for Digital UNIX that's free.
There was, some time ago, some interest expressed by Cygnus in doing gdb
support, and I answered a bunch of questions. I never heard anything
further from them, and I don't know what that means.

You can use the standard ladebug debugger (I won't even go into what
"ladebug" means, but basically it's just a pun on "ladybug"). You can also
buy the TotalView debugger from Dolphin Interconnect
(http://www.dolphinics.com). Both are quite nice, though with very
different sets of advantages and annoyances.

You can also use the standard Digital UNIX dbx. It will work with threads,
but not very smoothly. (It doesn't know about 2-level scheduling, for
example, and can't show the state of synchronization objects.)

