Sorry if this is repost, but it seems that my previus article was lost
somewhere on the way to news server.

I had Digital UNIX version 3.2 box with modem connected to leased
line and it worked just fine.  Couple days ago, I upgraded to Digital
UNIX version 4.0D.  After upgrade I experienced some strange problems
with modem.

First, when X server starts, it resets RS232 interface on my DEC 3000.
Since I have modem connected to it, it is not healty thing to do
(modem is connected to leased line, so I have slip connection running
24 hours a day).  If anybody knows how to prevent Xdec from touching
RS232, I'd appriciate any input.

Second problems is much more serius.  Slip simply does not work.
Configuration in rc.config is same as when I had Digital UNIX 3.2.
Relevent lines are:

NETDEV_1="sl0"
IFCONFIG1="localip-address-here remote-ip-address-here netmask 255.255.255.254"
SLIPTTY_1="+c -i tty00 38400"

Now, when machine boots (and after restarting slattach becose of the
problem with Xdec) things simply do not work.  If I try to ping the
remote machine (the one with remote-ip-address-here in IFCONFIG1 line)
send LED on modem blinks, but no response is sent back.  If I try to
ping from that remote machine, recv LED on modem blinks, but there is
no response sent from my local machine (which is very strange).

I also tryed to configure pppd, which also didn't work (LCP config
request failures).  Strange thing was that when I connected modem on
regular telephone line and *dialed* the number of modem which is in
the very same modem pool as the one on leased line, ppp worked without 
any problems.

If anybody outhere have working slip and/or ppp on Digital UNIX 4.0D
over leased line, I'd appritiate if they could send me any config
files or hints for either slip or ppp.

