Pedro Matias wrote:
> 
> Marc Ortega wrote in message <3641BE32.E1B80ECA@seneca.uab.es>...
> >Hi everyone,
> >I'm using X-Win32 to import a X session to a PC from a Digital Unix
> >machine, but I always get the message "Cannot obtain database
> >information from this terminal." Does anybody know where is the problem?
> >Should I configure anything on the DEC machine and what?
> >
> >Thank in advance,
> >Marc
> ...
> >
> I have used X-win32 (Starnet Communications) with DEC systems and never has
> any problem. I'm not sure I understand your question.
> Could you be a little more specific about what you're trying to do ?

The problem mentioned, has nothing to do with X Windows system. It has to do
with Enhanced Security (or C2). Every device that you try to log-in from MUST be
described in a terminals & devices databases. If not, you get denied with the
error message from above.

The databases are located in /etc/auth/system directory. Depending on the
version of Digital UNIX the files are:

+-----------------------+---------------+---------------+
|  Digital UNIX v.	|	file	|	type	|
+-----------------------+---------------+---------------+
+-----------------------+---------------+---------------+
| 3.2x and OSF/1	|	ttys	|	ASCII	|
+-----------------------+---------------+---------------+
| 4.0x			|	ttys.db	|	binary	|
+-----------------------+---------------+---------------+

In the version for 3.2, just edit the file and add an entry for an X Windows
terminal. Copy it from "local:0".

In version 4.0 you must use "edauth" command.

Nix.




