Marc Ortega (mortega@seneca.uab.es) wrote:
> Hi everyone,
> I'm using X-Win32 to import a X session to a PC from a Digital Unix
> machine, but I always get the message "Cannot obtain database
> information from this terminal." Does anybody know where is the problem?
> Should I configure anything on the DEC machine and what?

That's because you have enhanced security enabled.  You should add an
entry into terminal database similar to one for ":0" display for every
PC on which you want to use X-Win32.  If you have Digital UNIX 4.0,
you can use edauth command to do this.  For example (see the manual
page for details) create file /tmp/foobar that will look something
like this:

regoc\:0|regoc\:0.0:\
	:t_devname=regoc\:0:t_login_timeout#0:t_xdisplay:chkent:

  ^---- (this is TAB, not spaces).

Change "regoc:0" to whatever the name of PC you want to add into
database is.  Don't forget to escape ":" in display name with "\"
(like in example above).

Add the entry into database with:

# edauth -s -dt < /tmp/foobar

edauth command is located in /usr/tcb/bin.

"edauth -g" will print to stdout information from auth databases.  For 
example to see entry for ":0" from terminal database, use something
like:

# edauth -g -dt :0

