Digital UNIX 4.0D+latest patches.

We have a strange problem with name resolution and BIND, which only
affect
Digital UNIX, not e.g. Sun Solaris.

In our resolv.conf we list two name servers. The first one is a
"floating" IP address
which we can move around for better redundancy. The second one is a
"normal" IP address.

Resolv.conf:
domain  domain.se
nameserver      xxy.www.vvv.48  #virtual_dns1 (which also has IP name
othername_dns1)
nameserver      xxx.zzz.yyy.25  #dnsserver2



Initial connection to Digital servers have been very slow, and we have
tracked this
down to name resolution. Doing an nslookup from a digital server, and at
the same
time using snoop from the first name server gives this output from the
nslookup:
(takes 20-30 seconds to fail over to dnsserver2)

root@decserver1# nslookup someserver
*** Can't find server name for address xxy.www.vvv.48: Timed out
Server:  dnsserver2.domain.se
Address:  xxx.zzz.yyy.25

Name:    someserver.domain.se
Address:  xxy.www.vvv.34

And this is from the snoop:

othername_dns1# snoop src decserver1
Using device /dev/le (promiscuous mode)
decserver1.domain.se -> othername_dns1    TCP D=996 S=22
Ack=2536626715 Seq=862291997

Len=36 Win=33580
decserver1.domain.se -> virtual_dns1.domain.se DNS C port=1975
decserver1.domain.se -> othername_dns1    ICMP Destination unreachable
(Bad port)
decserver1.domain.se -> othername_dns1    TCP D=996 S=22
Ack=2536626735 Seq=862292033

Len=20 Win=33580
decserver1.domain.se -> virtual_dns1.domain.se DNS C port=1975
decserver1.domain.se -> othername_dns1    ICMP Destination unreachable
(Bad port)
decserver1.domain.se -> virtual_dns1.domain.se DNS C port=1975
decserver1.domain.se -> othername_dns1    ICMP Destination unreachable
(Bad port)
decserver1.domain.se -> virtual_dns1.domain.se DNS C port=1975
decserver1.domain.se -> othername_dns1    ICMP Destination unreachable
(Bad port)
decserver1.domain.se -> virtual_dns1.domain.se DNS C port=1977
decserver1.domain.se -> othername_dns1    ICMP Destination unreachable
(Bad port)

A ping from decserver1 to either virtual_dns1 or othername_dns1 also
shows one ICMP failure,

but seems to fail over to dnsserver2 almost at once.
Snoop says:

decserver1.ericsson.se -> virtual_dns1.ericsson.se DNS C port=2042
decserver1.ericsson.se -> othername_dns1    ICMP Destination unreachable
(Bad port)
decserver1.ericsson.se -> othername_dns1    TCP D=996 S=22
Ack=2536628655 Seq=862303509

Len=20 Win=33580
decserver1.ericsson.se -> virtual_dns1.ericsson.se ICMP Echo request


Doing the nslookup from a Solaris server works immediately, and a
corresponding snoop says:

sunserver.domain.se -> othername_dns1    TCP D=987 S=22
Ack=117062426 Seq=1441240807

Len=20 Win=8760
sunserver.domain.se -> othername_dns1    TCP D=987 S=22
Ack=117062446 Seq=1441240827

Len=36 Win=8760
sunserver.domain.se -> othername_dns1    TCP D=987 S=22
Ack=117062466 Seq=1441240863

Len=20 Win=8760
sunserver.domain.se -> virtual_dns1.domain.se DNS C port=34575
sunserver.domain.se -> virtual_dns1.domain.se DNS C port=34576
sunserver.domain.se -> othername_dns1    TCP D=987 S=22
Ack=117062466 Seq=1441240883

Len=156 Win=8760

Is there some bug in Digital's BIND that prevents us from using a
"virtual" name server?
If it works on Sun... Where does the ICMP error come from?

Any ideas?

