Knowhere_Man wrote:
> 
> We need to install two APC UPS (Smart UPS and Back UPS Pro). We have
> problems configuring the serial ports for this UPS.
> 
> For the Back UPS Pro the Powerchute Plus installation script displays a
> warning that indicates that the serial port is configured for local control
> and that it needs to be changed to modem control.

On DEC OSF/1 or Digital UNIX, PowerChute can communicate ONLY via smart
signaling cables. These "fit" only with Smart and Matrix UPS. It won't work with
Back-UPS.

You didn't say which Alpha you have. On servers you can usually set the type of
port control from firmware console. On "little" AlphaStations, well, I'm not
sure, haven't looked recently.

The other thing, that is most likely your problem, is the existance of a line in
your /etc/inittab, running getty, mgetty or ugetty on that port. You should find
it and change "respawn" into "off". Then issue "init q".

> Any ideas?
> 
> The smart UPS installation completes with no apparent problem but apparently
> theres no communication with the UPS. When running xpowerchute interface all
> options are greyed out.

Signaling MUST be smart (black cable), port MUST be free (no active getty on it)
and PowerCHUTE should be configured to use it.

Nix.




