>  I'm *so* spoiled by AIX's LVM that I'm now uncomfortable when
>  dealing with Linux.  One thing holding Linux back is the effort
>  to maintain some compatibility with MS-DOG's partitioning...

Being a big fan of LVM on AIX, I none-the-less do not really miss it on Linux. 
I suspect LVM would not be a big help on systems where there is only one hard 
drive, and it must be shared with one of the MS variants, which I suspect is 
still by far the largest percentage of implementations of Linux.

OTOH, for those who have large disk pools and want to get their feet wet with 
LVM on Linux, the 0.4 alpha code is available at
    ftp://ftp.msede.com/pub/linux/lvm
Not all functionality is included, as it is still in development. The author 
can be reached at
    linux.LVM@ez-darmstadt.telekom.de
He recently presented a paper at the Linux Kongress 1998 in Cologne on this 
effort, which is available at
    http://linux.msede.com/lvm/

